@startuml block_diagram
title K9-AIF with the OpenAI Agents SDK: where the adapter sits
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Client / event source" as Client

rectangle "K9-AIF Router\n(admit: authenticate, route by event_type)" as Router

rectangle "Native K9-AIF path" as Native {
  rectangle "Orchestrator\n(BaseOrchestrator)" as Orch
  rectangle "Squad\n(BaseSquad, YAML flow)" as Squad
  rectangle "Agents\n(BaseAgent, llm_invoke)" as Agents
}

rectangle "OpenAI path" as OAI {
  rectangle "OpenAIAgentsOrchestratorAdapter\n(is an Orchestrator: BaseOrchestrator + BaseAdapter)" as Adapter
  rectangle "OpenAI Agents SDK Runner\n(agent loop)" as Runner
  rectangle "OpenAI Agent + handoff agents\n(built by the adapter)" as OAgents
}

rectangle "Shared K9-AIF services (same config for both paths)" as Shared {
  rectangle "Shield governance\n(ingress, egress,\ntool args, tool results)" as Shield
  rectangle "Tool gate\n(registry, record checks,\nrules -> allow / deny / hil)" as Gate
  rectangle "HIL Orchestrator\n-> k9x HIL" as HIL
  rectangle "Model Router\n(eligibility, learned scores)" as MR
}

rectangle "Models\n(OpenAI, Azure OpenAI,\nOllama, vLLM)" as Models
rectangle "Tool handlers\n(registered capabilities)" as Tools

Client --> Router
Router --> Orch : event_type A
Router --> Adapter : event_type B

Orch --> Squad
Squad --> Agents

Adapter --> Runner : run()
Runner --> OAgents

Adapter ..> Shield : ingress, final output
OAgents ..> Shield : every tool call and result\n(K9ToolGuardrail)
OAgents ..> Gate : every tool call
OAgents ..> MR : every model call\n(K9ModelProvider)
Agents ..> Shield : governed by construction
Agents ..> MR : llm_invoke
Gate ..> HIL : review needed
MR --> Models
Gate --> Tools : allowed call

note right of OAI
  The adapter is one of the Router's
  orchestrators. The OpenAI Runner and
  its agents take the place of
  Squad -> Agent on this path.
  Hosted tools (web search, file search,
  code interpreter, hosted MCP) run on
  OpenAI servers: refused by default.
end note
@enduml
